3. Counter-Example: Gauge Drift (Constant Sheaf on K_3)

With \delta_0=\begin{pmatrix}-1&1&0\\0&-1&1\\1&0&-1\end{pmatrix}, \operatorname{Ker}(\delta_0)=\operatorname{span}(\mathbf{1}). Under s_{t+1}=s_t+\eta\mathbf{1}, c_{t+1}=c_t, so \Gamma(c_t)=0 and T(s_t)=T(s_0), while \|s_t\|_2\to\infty. This is a consensus zero mode, not a topological invariant of a non-trivial sheaf.

---

4. Lemma M0

For s=s_\parallel+s_\perp with s_\parallel\in\ker L_0 and s_\perp\in(\ker L_0)^\perp,

\|s_\perp\|_2\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_2(L_0)}}\|\delta_0 s\|_2=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_2(L_0)}}T(s).

Proof. By the spectral theorem, \|\delta_0 s\|_2^2=\langle L_0 s_\perp,s_\perp\rangle\geq\lambda_2(L_0)\|s_\perp\|_2^2. \blacksquare

