5. Resolution of Vulnerabilities

5.1 Sheaf and Obstruction

Monodromies restricted to fixed-subspace twists. For fixed-point-free twists (e.g., rotation in \mathbb{R}^2), H^1=0 and frustration is spectral, captured by \lambda_2(L_0)>0. Q1/Q2 compare cohomological vs spectral obstructions.

5.2 Energy Landscape

Variant A (Uncoupled). \mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{unc}}=\frac12 s^\top L_0 s+\frac{\mu}{2}\|P_\parallel s\|_2^2. Gradient descent gives s_{\parallel,t+1}=(1-\eta\mu)s_{\parallel,t}, s_{\perp,t+1}=(1-\eta\lambda_2(L_0))s_{\perp,t}. Corrects the v3.0 error (1-\eta(3+\mu)).

Variant B (Coupled). \mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{cpl}}=\frac12 s^\top L_0 s+\frac{\mu}{2}\|P_\parallel s\|_2^2+\nu\,s_\parallel^\top A s_\perp, with A:\ker L_0\to(\ker L_0)^\perp. Hessian H=\begin{pmatrix}\mu I&\nu A\\\nu A^\top&L_0|_{(\ker L_0)^\perp}\end{pmatrix}. H\succ0 iff \mu>\nu^2\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}^2/\lambda_2(L_0). Derived factors: \alpha=1-\eta\mu, \beta=1-\eta\lambda_2(L_0), L=\eta\nu\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}.

5.3 Annulus Falsifier

Replace C_6 with a triangulated annulus mesh (has 2-cells, so triangle penalty \sum_\sigma\|\delta_1 c\|_2^2 is non-trivial; has a global hole, so H^1\neq0). Construct c with zero circulation around each triangle (locally exact) but non-zero circulation around the hole. Then triangle penalty is zero while \Gamma(c)>0. This is non-vacuous.

5.4 Corrected Nonlinear Gradient

The v3.0 expression \delta_0^\top\circ\nabla U\circ\delta_0 is ill-typed: \delta_0:C^0\to C^1, \nabla U:C^0\to C^0, so \nabla U\circ\delta_0 is not composable. The correct gradient of \mathcal{E}(s)=\frac12\|\delta_0 s\|_2^2+U(s) is

\boxed{\nabla\mathcal{E}(s)=L_0 s+\nabla U(s).}

Theorem M0-S applies to the linearized dynamics around a critical point. Global stability for non-convex U is an open conjecture.

5.5 Thermodynamic Units and Coordinates

Unit correction. If entropy is in nats (natural log), the Landauer bound is k_BT\Delta S, not k_BT\ln2\cdot\Delta S. If in bits (\log_2), it is k_BT\ln2\cdot\Delta S. We use nats throughout and state Q\geq k_BT\max(0,S_t-S_{t+1}).

Coordinate dependence. Differential entropy is not invariant under coordinate transformations. The state space coordinates must be physically meaningful, derived from the friction tensor \zeta_{ij}=\partial^2\Phi/\partial\dot z^i\partial\dot z^j|_{\dot z=0}.

Speed-cost tradeoff. The static bound says nothing about rate. The finite-time excess work bound is

W_{\mathrm{ex}}\geq\frac{\mathcal{L}^2(\epsilon)}{\tau},

where \mathcal{L} is thermodynamic length. Faster protocols (smaller \tau) cost more.

