7. Thermodynamic Interpretation

Friction tensor. \zeta_{ij}=\partial^2\Phi/\partial\dot z^i\partial\dot z^j|_{\dot z=0}, inducing Riemannian metric on state space. Excess work W_{\mathrm{ex}}\geq\mathcal{L}^2/\tau.

Landauer bound. Q_t\geq k_BT\max(0,S_t-S_{t+1}) with S in nats. Stationary state: asymptotic per-step cost vanishes. Total stabilization cost Q_{\mathrm{total}}\geq k_BT\max(0,S_0-S_\infty). Faster gauge dissipation (larger \mu) implies larger total heat cost.

